REQ-001: The billing service shall verify the HMAC signature of every incoming webhook.
REQ-002: The billing service shall retry failed webhook deliveries up to five times.
REQ-003: The payment gateway shall record an audit log entry for every processed webhook.
REQ-004: While the payment provider is unavailable, the billing service shall queue retryable events.
REQ-005: While the system is in maintenance mode, the billing service shall reject incoming webhooks.
REQ-006: When a payment webhook is received, the billing service shall verify the HMAC signature.
REQ-007: When a refund is requested, the billing service shall issue a refund to the original payment method.
REQ-008: When an invoice is finalized, the billing service shall send the invoice to the customer.
REQ-009: Where dunning management is enabled, the billing service shall retry declined charges.
REQ-010: Where tax calculation is enabled, the billing service shall add sales tax to each invoice.
REQ-011: If the HMAC signature is invalid, then the billing service shall reject the webhook.
REQ-012: If the payment is declined, then the billing service shall notify the customer.
REQ-013: If the webhook timestamp is stale, then the billing service shall discard the event.
REQ-014: While the payment provider is unavailable, when a payment webhook is received, the billing service shall queue the event for retry.
REQ-015: When a payment webhook is received, if the HMAC signature is invalid, then the billing service shall reject the webhook.
